# 11g's reply to it (#2466): TTI_RPA, the opened locator (not the one sent),
# the mode as a ub8, the status.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8;
# OCILobFileExists, OCILobFileOpen and the like, called through ctypes) on
# Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started, reading
# BFILENAME('SEERDB_BFILE_DIR', 'pyoracle_bfile_test.txt'), 21 bytes. The TTC
# payload, without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset
# column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
